<title>SOUTH AFRICA: BA again cancels SAfrica flights due strike.</title>
<headline>BA again cancels SAfrica flights due strike.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Wednesday that disrupton caused by last week's 72-hour strike by cabin crew had forced it to again cancel flights to and from South Africa.</p>
<p>The cancelled services are BA57 to Johannesburg on Thursday night and BA59 to Cape Town on Friday night. As a result, BA56 from Johannesburg to London on Friday night and BA58 from Cape Town on Saturday night have had to be cancelled.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
